WEBVTT

00:00:01.090 --> 00:00:04.370
<i>The year is 2205 A.D.</i>

00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:13.510
<i>To annihilate the History Retrograde 
Army, who scheme to alter history,</i>

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:17.150
<i>we, who were born from swords,</i>

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:21.160
<i>engage in mortal combat today as well!</i>

00:00:23.030 --> 00:00:25.190
<i>So, wanna have a drink?</i>

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:43.370
<b>Touken Ranbu </b>Hanamaru<b></b>

00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:59.410
"This anime is about the 
stories of the Hanamaru days

00:01:59.410 --> 00:02:04.180
of a certain group of Sword 
Warriors in a certain citadel."

00:02:09.620 --> 00:02:11.890
So, you're all here now.

00:02:12.050 --> 00:02:13.920
The three spears are together.

00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:16.110
42 - Spear
<b> Nihongou</b>

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:16.110
41 - Spear 
<b>Tonbokiri</b>

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:16.110
What should the three of us do?

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:18.350
Isn't it obvious?

00:02:18.350 --> 00:02:19.860
Go drink some sake?

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:21.320
Fight, of course.

00:02:22.490 --> 00:02:23.770
I was joking.

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:24.990
Sure you were.

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:28.100
What are you laughing about?

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:30.000
Hurry and come over here!

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:38.660
Let's drink some sake.

00:02:40.710 --> 00:02:42.310
Amazing!

00:02:42.310 --> 00:02:43.840
I can see far away!

00:02:43.850 --> 00:02:46.850
Japan

00:02:43.850 --> 00:02:46.850
Otegine

00:02:43.850 --> 00:02:46.850
<b>The Blue Bird</b>

00:02:46.850 --> 00:02:52.100
The Blue Bird

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:52.430
And so, they all lived happily ever after.

00:02:52.690 --> 00:02:55.210
Th-The Blue Bird of Happiness...

00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:57.980
What a wonderful story.

00:02:58.120 --> 00:03:01.560
It's a good story book.
Did you get it from Master?

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:02.230
Yes.

00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:06.080
Thank you so much for reading 
it to me, Tonbokiri-san.

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:11.540
<b>The Blue Bird</b>

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:08.810
The lesson of this story is...

00:03:08.900 --> 00:03:09.920
That's right.

00:03:12.550 --> 00:03:15.060
Gokotai, where are you going?

00:03:15.390 --> 00:03:19.940
Th-There's something I want to get 
from my room. I'll be right back.

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:24.590
Tiger-kun?

00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:27.100
Hey.

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:29.330
What's the matter?

00:03:33.170 --> 00:03:34.850
I-I'm sorry.

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:38.010
Hey.

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:39.850
Gokotai.

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:43.390
What?

00:03:43.390 --> 00:03:44.620
That was kinda...

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:46.620
I feel bad for Gokotai.

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:48.730
Jeez, it's not like I could help it.

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:51.160
What couldn't you help?

00:03:52.150 --> 00:03:54.450
I'm not good with tigers.

00:03:55.310 --> 00:04:00.800
My former master had a tougher time with 
tigers than he did with enemy attacks,

00:03:56.880 --> 00:04:03.380
<b>Lord Steward
 Fukushima Saemon</b>

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:05.150
so when I see a tiger I'm forced to relive 
memories from a time I'd rather not.

00:04:05.380 --> 00:04:07.800
Even a tiger that small?

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:09.650
It's basically a cat.

00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:13.600
Gokotai told me he wants 
to get along with Nihongou.

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:18.700
"H-He's so cool because he 
has everything I lack."

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:22.730
You were surprised when
 the tiger jumped on you, right?

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:26.740
Then it is best that you tell 
him that and make amends.

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:28.720
Like I could do that.

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:31.730
A blue bird!

00:04:31.970 --> 00:04:33.310
Blue bird?

00:04:33.310 --> 00:04:35.200
It's definitely blue.

00:04:37.100 --> 00:04:39.660
Would that be the Blue Bird of Happiness?

00:04:39.660 --> 00:04:41.200
You think so?

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:43.620
A blue bird is a blue bird.

00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:46.360
Aren't good things supposed 
to happen if you catch one?

00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:50.090
He's totally ready to catch it.

00:04:50.440 --> 00:04:53.340
What, are you going to give it to Gokotai?

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:55.090
That's not it.

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:08.810
Otegine!

00:05:08.930 --> 00:05:09.900
Got a sec?

00:05:10.170 --> 00:05:11.340
What is it?

00:05:11.340 --> 00:05:12.880
Help me out here.

00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:17.740
I'm not any good at anything 
but stabbing though.

00:05:17.740 --> 00:05:18.430
Don't stab it!

00:05:18.430 --> 00:05:19.440
I'm not going to!

00:05:20.170 --> 00:05:21.850
Sit here.

00:05:25.310 --> 00:05:26.510
Now stand.

00:05:26.620 --> 00:05:28.920
G-Gonna ride on my shoulders?

00:05:29.710 --> 00:05:31.900
Okay, that's it.

00:05:36.350 --> 00:05:38.290
Ouch!

00:05:39.420 --> 00:05:41.200
I'm definitely catching it.

00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:43.080
Otegine, one more time!

00:05:43.330 --> 00:05:46.660
Hey now, are you gonna 
stand on my shoulders?

00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:49.050
Tough it out.

00:05:49.750 --> 00:05:51.390
Can you take one step forward?

00:05:51.390 --> 00:05:52.410
Forward?

00:05:57.070 --> 00:05:59.250
Who told you to dance?!

00:06:05.870 --> 00:06:07.380
This time for sure.

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:15.720
Dammit!

00:06:20.150 --> 00:06:21.640
You gotta be kidding.

00:06:21.810 --> 00:06:24.760
It's making fun of us now. Shall we give up?

00:06:25.160 --> 00:06:27.720
It's perched up there too high.

00:06:28.680 --> 00:06:30.240
Tonbokiri, got a sec?

00:06:30.380 --> 00:06:32.690
What? You want me, too?

00:06:33.430 --> 00:06:36.900
Listen, if we do it like this, 
we can reach that high, can't we?

00:06:36.900 --> 00:06:39.160
Is that even possible?

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:42.380
Why am I the one on the bottom?!

00:06:42.520 --> 00:06:47.340
This is nothing compared to the heavy thing 
you're usually carrying around, right?

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:50.630
It'll be tough with three.

00:06:50.940 --> 00:06:53.320
Are you all right, Otegine?

00:06:53.320 --> 00:06:54.790
Y-Yeah.

00:06:54.910 --> 00:06:57.170
Being in the middle is surprisingly tough.

00:06:59.750 --> 00:07:02.540
What's wrong, Otegine? Just one step closer!

00:07:02.540 --> 00:07:03.510
Right!

00:07:11.140 --> 00:07:12.790
Who told you to dance?!

00:07:12.790 --> 00:07:14.530
No one is dancing!

00:07:13.130 --> 00:07:15.320
That looks rather enjoyable.

00:07:15.950 --> 00:07:17.390
Just a bit more.

00:07:18.090 --> 00:07:19.480
One more step.

00:07:20.510 --> 00:07:22.670
Damn it!

00:07:22.820 --> 00:07:24.120
All right!

00:07:26.610 --> 00:07:27.420
I got it!

00:07:41.600 --> 00:07:43.320
Wait, Otegine!

00:07:43.320 --> 00:07:44.850
Stop!

00:07:44.850 --> 00:07:46.780
I can't!

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:55.480
Okay!

00:07:55.670 --> 00:07:57.630
The three spears are amazing!

00:08:00.300 --> 00:08:03.070
His eyes are drowsy and he looks comfy.

00:08:03.300 --> 00:08:05.510
I wonder if Hanatarou's sleepy.

00:08:05.510 --> 00:08:06.800
He's so cute.

00:08:15.510 --> 00:08:16.270
Ow!

00:08:18.630 --> 00:08:19.270
Kiyomitsu?

00:08:19.840 --> 00:08:20.780
Are you okay—

00:08:23.380 --> 00:08:24.120
Yasusada?!

00:08:30.530 --> 00:08:35.190
Kane-san, can you hang the washed sheets 
out to dry on that clothesline there?

00:08:35.550 --> 00:08:37.520
Sure, leave it to me.

00:08:41.050 --> 00:08:42.490
What the heck was that?

00:08:42.490 --> 00:08:43.620
No idea.

00:08:47.050 --> 00:08:49.860
Damn, why do I have to do this?

00:08:53.360 --> 00:08:54.380
What the?!

00:09:16.940 --> 00:09:17.990
What?!

00:09:31.710 --> 00:09:32.980
You bastards!

00:09:32.980 --> 00:09:34.330
Why are you messing around?!

00:09:38.070 --> 00:09:39.170
Over there!

00:09:39.170 --> 00:09:40.900
It's over by the pond!

00:09:41.980 --> 00:09:43.680
Fly, Otegine!

00:09:43.780 --> 00:09:45.650
Don't be crazy!

00:09:45.730 --> 00:09:46.850
The clothesline!

00:09:46.850 --> 00:09:48.460
Use the clothesline!

00:09:48.850 --> 00:09:50.380
I told you!

00:09:50.380 --> 00:09:56.310
I only have a talent for stabbing things!

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:03.360
I'll get it this time!

00:10:04.050 --> 00:10:04.790
Gotcha!

00:10:07.450 --> 00:10:09.800
You've gotta be kidding!

00:10:21.110 --> 00:10:22.510
We can't let it perch there!

00:10:22.510 --> 00:10:25.110
My spear is sharp enough 
that even a dragonfly

00:10:25.110 --> 00:10:26.930
perching there will be cut in half!

00:10:33.470 --> 00:10:35.150
It perched!

00:10:39.980 --> 00:10:42.110
I think this is impossible for us to do.

00:10:43.630 --> 00:10:46.200
I got to see something interesting.

00:11:02.330 --> 00:11:03.530
Gokotai?

00:11:03.800 --> 00:11:05.230
U-Um...

00:11:05.420 --> 00:11:07.420
What do you have there?

00:11:08.230 --> 00:11:10.390
A-A protection charm.

00:11:10.890 --> 00:11:14.230
Th-They've been pretty popular 
around here lately.

00:11:14.460 --> 00:11:17.770
You can put whatever you like inside it.

00:11:17.950 --> 00:11:23.420
I-I thought you might not have one, 
Nihongou-san, since you just arrived.

00:11:23.900 --> 00:11:25.700
Please let me borrow that.

00:11:26.050 --> 00:11:27.500
Ah, okay.

00:11:36.600 --> 00:11:38.550
H-Here you are.

00:11:39.280 --> 00:11:40.580
Thanks.

00:11:41.750 --> 00:11:44.810
Happiness is always right nearby.

00:11:45.390 --> 00:11:47.530
That's the lesson of this story.

00:11:47.530 --> 00:11:51.240
Y-Your acrobatics just now were enjoyable.

00:11:51.240 --> 00:11:52.240
Acrobatics?

00:11:52.330 --> 00:11:54.970
D-Do you think you could do it again?

00:11:55.320 --> 00:11:56.930
Absolutely not!

00:12:06.530 --> 00:12:08.730
Brilliant, brilliant.

00:12:10.700 --> 00:12:12.960
<b>Touken Ranbu </b>Hanamaru<b></b>

00:12:22.440 --> 00:12:25.070
Do you hear that voice?

00:12:25.400 --> 00:12:26.460
I hear it.

00:12:27.140 --> 00:12:29.040
Who is it at this hour?

00:12:29.270 --> 00:12:30.880
What if it's a ghost?

00:12:33.140 --> 00:12:34.300
It's coming this way.

00:12:36.270 --> 00:12:37.460
Nii-san...

00:12:38.060 --> 00:12:39.130
Akita?

00:12:39.610 --> 00:12:41.090
What's the matter, Akita?

00:12:41.090 --> 00:12:42.340
Why are you crying?

00:12:43.350 --> 00:12:45.000
There was a ghost.

00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:46.350
A ghost?!

00:12:46.970 --> 00:12:48.840
I was on my way to the bathroom,

00:12:49.110 --> 00:12:54.290
and there was a floating white shadow, 
walking without making any steps.

00:12:55.050 --> 00:12:58.940
I was so scared, but I ran 
after it, and then—

00:13:00.880 --> 00:13:02.880
Why did you shout?

00:13:02.880 --> 00:13:04.540
I thought it'd be a good time.

00:13:04.540 --> 00:13:06.610
Y-You scared me.

00:13:06.770 --> 00:13:09.060
So, you chased after it?

00:13:09.320 --> 00:13:12.290
I immediately lost sight of it.

00:13:12.740 --> 00:13:14.890
It was a ghost!

00:13:15.610 --> 00:13:17.130
S-Scary.

00:13:17.510 --> 00:13:19.890
Something like that is in the citadel?

00:13:20.150 --> 00:13:21.890
What a frightening story.

00:13:21.890 --> 00:13:23.530
Isn't this pretty bad?

00:13:23.530 --> 00:13:25.060
Shouldn't we wake Ichi-nii?

00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:27.420
No, we'll figure this out ourselves.

00:13:28.050 --> 00:13:29.180
That's right.

00:13:29.180 --> 00:13:32.820
Since we already bragged to Ichi-nii 
about how much stronger we've gotten.

00:13:33.040 --> 00:13:34.830
I-I guess you're right.

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:36.430
We can do it without Ichi-nii.

00:13:37.130 --> 00:13:38.500
It's scary!

00:13:38.750 --> 00:13:42.290
However, we have no leads on how to go 
about finding this ghost or whatever.

00:13:42.500 --> 00:13:44.550
It'd be nice to have some kind of help.

00:13:44.900 --> 00:13:46.670
We'll go get someone,

00:13:46.780 --> 00:13:48.500
since we know who is qualified.

00:13:48.850 --> 00:13:49.950
You all wait here.

00:13:51.900 --> 00:13:53.730
Who are they going to get?

00:13:54.270 --> 00:13:56.440
Probably Nikkari Aoe.

00:13:56.440 --> 00:13:57.970
Nikkari-san?

00:13:59.660 --> 00:14:06.300
His name is based on an old story where he 
cut the spirit of an eerily laughing woman.

00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:07.650
He might be useful.

00:14:08.540 --> 00:14:10.680
Nikkari-san! I see!

00:14:10.680 --> 00:14:14.260
Then let's have Nikkari Aoe hurry 
up and cut down the ghost!

00:14:14.740 --> 00:14:15.760
You're right.

00:14:18.840 --> 00:14:20.580
Nikkari-san.

00:14:20.770 --> 00:14:22.600
Nikkari Aoe-san.

00:14:23.120 --> 00:14:25.230
What is it at this late hour?

00:14:25.230 --> 00:14:26.800
An emergency situation has occurred.

00:14:27.070 --> 00:14:28.310
Is that so?

00:14:28.500 --> 00:14:30.390
Has a ghost appeared or something?

00:14:30.390 --> 00:14:31.220
It has.

00:14:31.930 --> 00:14:34.540
Akita said he saw a ghost.

00:14:34.810 --> 00:14:39.180
I've never heard of a ghost 
in this citadel before now.

00:14:39.610 --> 00:14:40.930
We need your help.

00:14:42.130 --> 00:14:42.950
Very well.

00:14:43.130 --> 00:14:45.450
Leave the ghosts and such to me.

00:14:47.850 --> 00:14:49.620
Sorry for bothering you so late.

00:14:49.870 --> 00:14:53.200
I, too, am interested in 
the identity of the ghost.

00:14:53.570 --> 00:14:55.720
I'm sure it will be plenty of fun.

00:14:55.720 --> 00:14:58.880
Let's form a Ghost Extermination Rangers!

00:14:59.110 --> 00:15:01.070
Ghost Extermination Rangers?

00:15:01.770 --> 00:15:03.190
Continue after me!

00:15:03.190 --> 00:15:05.670
Namazuo: Navy Blue, reporting!

00:15:09.220 --> 00:15:10.260
Huh?

00:15:10.640 --> 00:15:12.750
Ah, we're supposed to say a color, right?

00:15:13.180 --> 00:15:14.930
Hakata: Gold!

00:15:15.130 --> 00:15:16.710
Midare: Pink!

00:15:16.710 --> 00:15:18.170
I'm pink, too!

00:15:18.340 --> 00:15:19.830
I'm black.

00:15:19.970 --> 00:15:20.980
Honebami: Silver.

00:15:20.980 --> 00:15:22.400
Yagen: Purple.

00:15:22.580 --> 00:15:23.830
Maeda: Yellow.

00:15:23.830 --> 00:15:25.020
Hirano: Brown.

00:15:25.020 --> 00:15:26.600
G-Gokotai: White.

00:15:26.980 --> 00:15:29.010
And Nikkari is green.

00:15:29.010 --> 00:15:30.450
Ah, wait a minute!

00:15:30.450 --> 00:15:31.990
We don't have a red or blue?

00:15:31.990 --> 00:15:33.480
Oh well, we'll be fine.

00:15:33.480 --> 00:15:34.550
That's right.

00:15:35.090 --> 00:15:38.270
Okay, the Ghost Extermination 
Rangers with Nikkari Aoe

00:15:38.270 --> 00:15:41.230
and the ten Awataguchi 
swords has been formed!

00:15:49.280 --> 00:15:51.480
Everyone has their candles, right?

00:15:52.000 --> 00:15:56.650
Now then, we'll split into groups. If you 
find the ghost, come get me immediately.

00:15:56.650 --> 00:15:58.720
I-I'm scared.

00:15:58.720 --> 00:15:59.980
Me, too.

00:15:59.980 --> 00:16:01.470
It'll be okay, let's go.

00:16:01.730 --> 00:16:02.500
Right.

00:16:05.390 --> 00:16:08.040
The Hakata Security Company is not cheap!

00:16:08.040 --> 00:16:10.110
Don't mess around at a time like this.

00:16:10.110 --> 00:16:11.030
Shall we go?

00:16:11.480 --> 00:16:12.920
A-All right!

00:16:13.400 --> 00:16:14.820
Namazuo, Honebami.

00:16:15.120 --> 00:16:16.390
Yes!

00:16:16.790 --> 00:16:19.030
I have a good idea.

00:16:19.690 --> 00:16:22.240
We'll lay out a net joined to a pulley here,

00:16:22.590 --> 00:16:26.570
and when the ghost comes, 
we pull on the rope and catch it.

00:16:27.160 --> 00:16:29.790
Can you even catch a ghost 
with something like that?

00:16:30.150 --> 00:16:33.880
I can't sense its presence,

00:16:33.880 --> 00:16:37.000
so I'm quite interested
in trying to capture it.

00:16:37.650 --> 00:16:40.560
Seeing a ghost's scared face 
will also be amusing, won't it?

00:16:40.560 --> 00:16:43.000
That's if it goes that easily.

00:16:44.640 --> 00:16:46.400
N-Nikkari-san!

00:16:49.930 --> 00:16:51.450
Over here.

00:16:59.180 --> 00:17:01.900
<i>There really is a ghost here?</i>

00:17:03.740 --> 00:17:06.540
<i>And to think we'd find it so easily.</i>

00:17:09.550 --> 00:17:10.990
Tsurumaru-san?

00:17:10.990 --> 00:17:12.850
What is it, Nikkari Aoe?

00:17:13.860 --> 00:17:16.280
A-And you have Mr. Fox with you?

00:17:16.280 --> 00:17:20.190
Yes, it seems the fox strayed into my room.

00:17:20.260 --> 00:17:25.050
I was wondering why it was so hot, and found this fuzzball on my face.

00:17:25.490 --> 00:17:28.260
So he mixed up the rooms.

00:17:29.260 --> 00:17:32.260
It takes a lot to surprise me.

00:17:32.380 --> 00:17:34.630
Surprises are necessary in life.

00:17:34.920 --> 00:17:39.040
Now then, I'm going back to bed.

00:17:44.890 --> 00:17:46.230
Nikkari-san!

00:17:47.590 --> 00:17:50.190
I-I heard the ghost's voice.

00:17:50.520 --> 00:17:51.300
Voice?

00:17:53.060 --> 00:17:54.990
The ghost was speaking?

00:17:54.990 --> 00:17:57.400
It was saying, "One, two, three."

00:17:57.730 --> 00:18:02.470
It sounds just like the ghost
of Okiku, counting her plates.

00:18:02.470 --> 00:18:03.620
Ghost?!

00:18:04.370 --> 00:18:09.690
Seven, eight...

00:18:08.380 --> 00:18:10.470
Is someone there?

00:18:10.740 --> 00:18:12.480
Nine...

00:18:12.840 --> 00:18:14.990
I'll slice you if you don't answer.

00:18:15.880 --> 00:18:18.470
Ten!

00:18:19.210 --> 00:18:21.500
Why are you doing pull-ups at this hour?

00:18:21.500 --> 00:18:23.820
I couldn't sleep.

00:18:24.150 --> 00:18:26.920
Okay, only 970 to go!

00:18:26.920 --> 00:18:30.290
If you do that 970 more times, it'll 
be morning by the time you're done.

00:18:30.620 --> 00:18:32.510
Then, will you train with me?

00:18:34.220 --> 00:18:36.250
It's lively at night.

00:18:38.210 --> 00:18:39.420
We found it.

00:18:39.630 --> 00:18:42.130
N-Nikkari-san!

00:18:45.900 --> 00:18:46.880
Where?

00:18:52.720 --> 00:18:55.320
That's a rather big ghost, isn't it?

00:18:58.200 --> 00:19:00.560
What are you doing?

00:19:03.630 --> 00:19:06.870
I shouldn't cook when I'm drunk.

00:19:06.870 --> 00:19:09.930
Oh, what's everyone doing together?

00:19:10.240 --> 00:19:11.360
Jirou-san!

00:19:11.360 --> 00:19:13.450
What are you making this late at night?!

00:19:15.490 --> 00:19:16.950
Tomatoes?

00:19:17.280 --> 00:19:19.300
My snacks are done!

00:19:19.300 --> 00:19:21.420
I'm going to have another drink over there.

00:19:21.650 --> 00:19:23.880
I'll clean up later!

00:19:27.140 --> 00:19:28.450
Look over there!

00:19:28.450 --> 00:19:29.920
A white ghost!

00:19:35.340 --> 00:19:37.340
It's finally my turn.

00:19:38.880 --> 00:19:40.620
Come on out, now.

00:19:41.560 --> 00:19:43.350
Don't be shy.

00:19:47.080 --> 00:19:48.120
Kasen?

00:19:48.510 --> 00:19:50.560
What in the world are you doing here?

00:19:51.060 --> 00:19:55.250
As you can see, I'm drying 
this cloth that I washed.

00:19:55.690 --> 00:19:57.150
This late at night?

00:19:57.650 --> 00:20:00.390
This cloth belongs to Yamanbagiri.

00:20:00.740 --> 00:20:04.140
Yamanbagiri never lets this 
out of his sight during the day,

00:20:04.140 --> 00:20:07.840
so I use this opportunity
when he's asleep to wash it.

00:20:08.510 --> 00:20:13.170
Though a pure white cloth is the most 
elegant, he might take notice.

00:20:13.730 --> 00:20:16.180
The trick is not to clean it too much.

00:20:16.180 --> 00:20:18.050
So it was thanks to Kasen, then?

00:20:18.050 --> 00:20:22.210
That's why it smelled nice, like fabric 
softener, even though it was so dirty.

00:20:22.600 --> 00:20:24.660
Did I clean it too much?

00:20:25.200 --> 00:20:26.960
Maybe I should dirty it a bit more.

00:20:29.070 --> 00:20:31.620
Which means there was no ghost.

00:20:32.180 --> 00:20:34.660
Akita Toushirou was just seeing things.

00:20:34.960 --> 00:20:38.200
We did it! We finally caught the ghost!

00:20:39.690 --> 00:20:43.110
I didn't think you'd do it, but 
did you really set up the trap?

00:20:47.190 --> 00:20:49.070
It's the ghost I saw!

00:20:49.070 --> 00:20:50.270
Let's see.

00:20:50.710 --> 00:20:53.280
The face of the ghost is...

00:20:54.320 --> 00:20:56.320
Kousetsu Samonji?

00:20:56.560 --> 00:20:58.440
K-Kousetsu-san?

00:20:58.880 --> 00:21:03.020
It appears that I have 
caused quite a commotion.

00:21:04.620 --> 00:21:09.960
I had gone to the bathroom with Osayo, 
but because of the recent room change,

00:21:10.080 --> 00:21:14.890
I lost track of how to get back, 
and was looking for our room.

00:21:15.920 --> 00:21:18.000
That's when they caught you.

00:21:18.120 --> 00:21:19.130
I'm sorry.

00:21:19.130 --> 00:21:20.070
I'll get you down now.

00:21:20.070 --> 00:21:23.490
No, that's fine, you can leave it.

00:21:23.490 --> 00:21:24.700
Why is that?

00:21:25.350 --> 00:21:28.130
Ah, your little brother is there.

00:21:28.460 --> 00:21:30.280
He's deep asleep.

00:21:30.850 --> 00:21:35.570
If you think of this as bedding, 
it is not entirely uncomfortable.

00:21:36.180 --> 00:21:38.680
Osayo also seems comfortable.

00:21:39.000 --> 00:21:41.180
We'll stay like this just a bit longer.

00:21:42.180 --> 00:21:43.120
I see.

00:21:45.090 --> 00:21:46.620
Feel better now?

00:21:46.620 --> 00:21:48.960
Okay, let's all go back to bed.

00:21:48.960 --> 00:21:50.500
Okay!

00:21:50.500 --> 00:21:52.290
Thank you for your help.

00:21:52.590 --> 00:21:55.780
The Ghost Extermination Rangers' 
mission is now complete!

00:21:55.950 --> 00:21:59.400
As green, it was a very meaningful time.

00:21:59.580 --> 00:22:00.760
Good night.

00:22:00.980 --> 00:22:01.920
<i>Three.</i>

00:22:02.520 --> 00:22:03.810
Good night.

00:22:03.810 --> 00:22:04.570
<i>Four...</i>

00:22:04.570 --> 00:22:05.840
Night.

00:22:05.840 --> 00:22:06.820
<i>Five.</i>

00:22:06.820 --> 00:22:07.890
Good night.

00:22:07.890 --> 00:22:09.340
<i>Six, seven.</i>

00:22:08.660 --> 00:22:10.550
G-Good night.

00:22:10.550 --> 00:22:11.130
<i>Eight.</i>

00:22:11.490 --> 00:22:12.700
Night.

00:22:12.700 --> 00:22:13.350
<i>Nine.</i>

00:22:13.350 --> 00:22:14.540
Good night.

00:22:14.540 --> 00:22:15.240
<i>Ten.</i>

00:22:15.240 --> 00:22:16.590
Good night.

00:22:16.590 --> 00:22:17.620
<i>Eleven...</i>

00:22:18.090 --> 00:22:18.950
Huh?!

00:22:19.720 --> 00:22:21.430
<i>There are eleven?!</i>

00:22:25.550 --> 00:22:27.990
<i>Akita said he saw a ghost, but...</i>

00:22:27.990 --> 00:22:29.820
<i>But in the end there wasn't one.</i>

00:22:29.820 --> 00:22:32.590
<i>You were half asleep and
just thought you saw one, right, Akita?</i>

00:22:32.590 --> 00:22:34.850
<i>It would be nice if that were true.</i>

00:22:34.940 --> 00:22:36.430
<i>It was like a courage test.</i>

00:22:36.430 --> 00:22:38.420
<i>I-It was scary.</i>

00:22:38.630 --> 00:22:41.380
<i>But it all worked out because
Nikkari-san helped us.</i>

00:22:41.380 --> 00:22:42.270
<i>You helped us.</i>

00:22:42.270 --> 00:22:43.650
<i>Thank you.</i>

00:22:43.650 --> 00:22:46.410
<i>Now, let's hurry back to our room and sleep.</i>

00:22:52.250 --> 00:22:53.800
<i>Is it a scary story?</i>

00:22:56.090 --> 00:22:57.380
<i>I'm going to sleep.</i>

00:22:59.730 --> 00:23:01.500
<i>That's unsettling.</i>

00:23:03.470 --> 00:23:05.320
<i>It's an unusual story, isn't it?</i>

00:23:06.890 --> 00:23:08.810
<i>Ghosts don't exist, do they?</i>

00:23:09.780 --> 00:23:12.330
<i>I'll punish anyone suspicious!</i>

00:23:13.470 --> 00:23:15.490
<i>P-Please stop.</i>

00:23:17.390 --> 00:23:19.550
<i>Staying up this late is bad for our skin.</i>

00:23:21.280 --> 00:23:23.020
<i>Come on, let's sleep.</i>

00:23:24.850 --> 00:23:26.420
<i>Will I be able to sleep?</i>

00:23:28.740 --> 00:23:29.880
<i>Good night.</i>

00:23:29.880 --> 00:23:31.140
<i>There's one too many.</i>

00:23:54.990 --> 00:23:59.990
<b>More Hanamaru Next Week!</b>
